data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"BM25 is a weighted count of query terms. Three ideas do the work. A term's weight grows with how rare it\nis across the collection (the idf). Its count saturates: the tenth occurrence adds less than the second.\nA longer document is discounted, because a long text contains more words by chance. The constants k1 and\nb set how strong the saturation and the length discount are."},"hints_note":null}

